  "outlook": "\u201cWe continue to see strong momentum in our markets, as evidenced by the 50% improvement in both U.S. municipal and industrial orders so far this year,\u201d noted Sherman. \u201cWith a record backlog, demand for our products is outpacing the current capacity of our supply chain. During the third quarter, delays in receiving chassis were more prevalent than we had anticipated, causing increased disruption to our production schedules. We expect that the volatile supply chain environment will continue for the rest of the year and, therefore, we are adjusting our full-year adjusted EPS outlook to a new range of $1.68 to $1.78. With good access to labor, and anticipated benefits from recent organic growth investments and acquisitions, we remain encouraged by the long-term opportunities for our businesses, which would be further boosted by infrastructure legislation recently passed by Congress.\u201d"
 },
